{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"7517655439b8ca9759c61715c6770a7486e09406415e36a9a41f70669e009ab5","slug":"chapters.preface.what-is-programming","location":"/chapters/preface/what_is_programming.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Was ist Programmieren?","numbering":{"title":{"enabled":true,"offset":1},"equation":{"enabled":true,"continue":true},"heading_1":{"enabled":false},"heading_2":{"enabled":false},"heading_3":{"enabled":false},"heading_4":{"enabled":false},"heading_5":{"enabled":false},"heading_6":{"enabled":false}},"content_includes_title":false,"keywords":["python","chemistry"],"thumbnail":"/python_for_chemists/build/computer_figma-473e388bf29e2ca0c0e61c94df30a63d.pdf","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"what_is_programming.md","url":"/python_for_chemists/build/what_is_programming-cd30efc472ce58a86aba275532e26ca5.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","kind":"caution","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under Construction","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"HzwMXyFjUR"}],"key":"h8zpnsevWk"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Diese Seite befindet sich noch im Aufbau. Bitte haben Sie etwas Geduld, bis sie vollständig ist.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"BUu9Qa28za"}],"key":"wI4qYl25Ks"}],"key":"nWkmkKTwsy"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Programmieren bedeutet, einem Computer Anweisungen so aufzuschreiben, dass er sie Schritt für Schritt ausführen kann. Diese Anweisungen werden in einer Textdatei gespeichert und bilden zusammen ein Programm.","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"dEZirk57LO"}],"key":"cQt9JbEaii"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ein Computer verarbeitet Informationen nach festen Regeln. Er “versteht” nicht, was wir meinen, sondern führt nur genau die Befehle aus, die ihm gegeben werden.","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"a3SaiWURtD"}],"key":"UyoyjCDcA1"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Python ist eine Programmiersprache, also eine bestimmte Art, solche Anweisungen zu formulieren. Sie ist gut lesbar und deshalb besonders geeignet, um die Grundlagen des Programmierens zu lernen.","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"czy9rCF5XC"}],"key":"ns1f22UidL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wenn Sie ein Python-Programm starten, liest der Computer den Code und arbeitet die Befehle der Reihe nach ab. So lassen sich Berechnungen automatisieren, Daten auswerten und wiederholbare Abläufe zuverlässig ausführen.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"pPUCCwbzXb"}],"key":"kQEyfS9cE9"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/python_for_chemists/build/computer_figma-473e388bf29e2ca0c0e61c94df30a63d.pdf","align":"center","key":"agLmTTWtt7","urlSource":"../../assets/figures/preface/computer_figma.pdf"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"FT57OiSvUw"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/python_for_chemists/build/python_figma-bc887049a808d7bbb5d7eed97006ce91.pdf","align":"center","key":"Q5fXzySb83","urlSource":"../../assets/figures/preface/python_figma.pdf"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"t59GB6PSXQ"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/python_for_chemists/build/code_figma-babd6a0a3a3a5367d531e8f05a3c8